<body>

<div class="container">

  <h1>CTR<span>.</span> Autofill</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">📖 Complete Tutorial – How to Use This Tool (v3.0)</div>

  <!-- ===== SECTION 1: OVERVIEW ===== -->
  <h2>🔍 What Does This Tool Do?</h2>
  <p>
    This tool helps you <strong>automatically fill crew forms</strong> for different destinations. You upload a PDF from the <strong>CrewTripReport</strong> system, and the tool:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>📋 <strong>Extracts</strong> all crew names, ranks, and IDs from the PDF.</li>
    <li>📄 <strong>Generates</strong> A4‑sized forms with each crew member's name, rank, and ID placed in the correct slots.</li>
    <li>🖨️ <strong>Lets you print</strong> the forms directly or save them as PNG or PDF.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>💡 Why use this?</strong> Instead of manually writing every name on every form, you do it once – the tool does the rest.
  </div>

  <!-- ===== SECTION 2: GETTING STARTED ===== -->
  <h2>🚀 Getting Started – Step by Step</h2>

  <div class="step-card">
    <div><span class="step-number">1</span> <strong>Upload a PDF</strong></div>
    <p style="margin-top:6px; margin-bottom:0;">
      Click the big blue <span class="btn-upload-demo" style="font-size:13px; padding:8px 20px;">📎 Choose File</span> button and select your <strong>CrewTripReport PDF</strong>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-card">
    <div><span class="step-number">2</span> <strong>Wait for auto‑parse</strong></div>
    <p style="margin-top:6px; margin-bottom:0;">
      The tool will automatically read the PDF and extract the crew list. You'll see a message: <span style="color:var(--green);">✅ Parsed OK</span>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-card">
    <div><span class="step-number">3</span> <strong>Select your destination</strong></div>
    <p style="margin-top:6px; margin-bottom:0;">
      From the dropdown, choose where you are flying to. Supported destinations:
      <strong>BOM, DEL, HYD, BLR, AMD, ATQ</strong>.
      This tells the tool which forms to generate.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-card">
    <div><span class="step-number">4</span> <strong>Generate forms</strong></div>
    <p style="margin-top:6px; margin-bottom:0;">
      Click the <span class="button-demo btn-blue">⚡ Generate Forms</span> button.
      The tool will load the correct templates for your destination and place every crew member into the right slots.
      <br><strong>Note:</strong> If a template has multiple Captains, you'll be prompted to select the <strong>Pilot In Charge (PIC)</strong> – the chosen Captain's name will appear on every page of that form.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="step-card">
    <div><span class="step-number">5</span> <strong>Review & print</strong></div>
    <p style="margin-top:6px; margin-bottom:0;">
      Each form appears in its own section. You can <strong>print</strong> each form separately or download all as PNG/PDF.
      Use the <strong>fine‑tune sliders</strong> to adjust text positions if needed.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- ===== SECTION 3: ALL BUTTONS EXPLAINED ===== -->
  <h2>🔘 All Buttons & What They Do</h2>

  <h3>📄 Parser Card</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Button / Element</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="btn-upload-demo" style="font-size:13px; padding:6px 16px;">📎 Choose File</span></td>
      <td>Opens your file browser to select a PDF. This is the <strong>main way</strong> to import data.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="button-demo btn-gray">⚡ Parse PDF Report</span></td>
      <td>If you pasted text instead of uploading a file, click this to parse it.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="button-demo btn-gray">Clear</span></td>
      <td>Clears the text area and resets the parser.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;color:var(--accent);">✅ file.pdf loaded</span></td>
      <td>Shows the name of the file you uploaded (turns green when loaded).</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h3>📄 A4 Forms Card</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Button / Element</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Destination dropdown</strong></td>
      <td>Choose your destination (BOM, DEL, HYD, BLR, AMD, ATQ). This selects which forms to generate.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="button-demo btn-blue">⚡ Generate Forms</span></td>
      <td>Loads the templates for your destination and places all crew onto the forms. If multiple Captains exist, you'll be asked to choose the PIC.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="button-demo btn-green">🖨️ Print A4 Sheets</span></td>
      <td>Opens a print window with <strong>only this form's pages</strong> – perfect for checking alignment.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="button-demo btn-blue" style="background:var(--accent);">📋 Copy Slots</span></td>
      <td>Copies the adjusted slot coordinates to your clipboard – useful for advanced users.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="button-demo btn-blue">⬇️ Download All PNGs</span></td>
      <td>Downloads <strong>every page</strong> as separate PNG images (one after another).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="button-demo btn-green">⬇️ Download All PDF</span></td>
      <td>Downloads <strong>all pages</strong> combined into one PDF file.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h3>🎛️ Fine‑Tune Controls</h3>
  <p>
    Each form has its own set of sliders. These let you adjust where the text appears on the page – <strong>without</strong> changing the original template.
  </p>

  <div class="grid-2">
    <div style="background:var(--surface2); padding:12px 16px; border-radius:var(--radius-sm); border:1px solid var(--border);">
      <strong>Name X</strong><br>
      <span style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted);">Moves the <strong>name</strong> left (negative) or right (positive).</span>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface2); padding:12px 16px; border-radius:var(--radius-sm); border:1px solid var(--border);">
      <strong>Name Y</strong><br>
      <span style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted);">Moves the <strong>name</strong> up (negative) or down (positive).</span>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface2); padding:12px 16px; border-radius:var(--radius-sm); border:1px solid var(--border);">
      <strong>Rank X</strong><br>
      <span style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted);">Moves the <strong>rank</strong> left or right. (Only shown if rank slots exist.)</span>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface2); padding:12px 16px; border-radius:var(--radius-sm); border:1px solid var(--border);">
      <strong>Rank Y</strong><br>
      <span style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted);">Moves the <strong>rank</strong> up or down.</span>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface2); padding:12px 16px; border-radius:var(--radius-sm); border:1px solid var(--border);">
      <strong>Number X / Number Y</strong><br>
      <span style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted);">Moves the <strong>row number</strong> (1, 2, 3…) left/right or up/down. (Only if numbering slots exist.)</span>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface2); padding:12px 16px; border-radius:var(--radius-sm); border:1px solid var(--border);">
      <strong>Crew ID X / Crew ID Y</strong><br>
      <span style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted);">Moves the <strong>crew ID</strong> left/right or up/down. (Only if ID slots exist.)</span>
    </div>
    <div style="background:var(--surface2); padding:12px 16px; border-radius:var(--radius-sm); border:1px solid var(--border); grid-column: span 2;">
      <strong>Font Size</strong><br>
      <span style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted);">Makes all text on this form <strong>larger</strong> (positive) or <strong>smaller</strong> (negative).</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>✏️ Pro tip:</strong> You can also <strong>type</strong> a number directly into the box next to each slider for precise adjustments.
  </div>

  <!-- ===== NEW: FORM BUILDER ===== -->
  <h2>🧱 Hidden Developer Tools – Form Builder</h2>
  <p>
    The tool includes a <strong>Form Builder</strong> that lets you design your own templates. It is hidden by default – you unlock it by tapping the <span style="font-size:24px;">👷</span> emoji at the <strong>very bottom of the page</strong> <strong>7 times</strong>.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Each tap shows a toast message with remaining taps.</li>
    <li>After the 7th tap, the <strong>Form Builder card</strong> appears.</li>
    <li>You can upload a canvas (template background), define slot positions for Name, Rank, Number, Crew ID, and PIC slots, and export the code to use in the main app.</li>
    <li>Your saved templates are stored locally in your browser.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="note">
    <strong>🔒 This is a developer feature</strong> – it's meant for advanced users who want to create new templates for destinations not yet supported.
  </div>

  <h3>Using the Form Builder</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Unlock it</strong> with 7 taps on the 👷 at the bottom.</li>
    <li><strong>Upload a canvas</strong> – a PNG or JPG image of the blank form (A4 landscape recommended).</li>
    <li><strong>Adjust slot parameters</strong> – each slot type (Name, Rank, etc.) has its own settings: start X/Y, rows, gap, width, height, and font size.</li>
    <li><strong>Click on the canvas</strong> to set the Start X/Y for the selected slot type – the tool automatically uses the clicked coordinates.</li>
    <li><strong>Enable PIC Top Page</strong> if you want a Captain to appear on every page.</li>
    <li><strong>Save</strong> your template, then <strong>Export Code</strong> – copy the generated slot code and paste it into the main <code>TEMPLATES</code> object in <code>CTR.html</code>.</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- ===== SECTION 4: PRINTING ===== -->
  <h2>🖨️ How to Print the Forms</h2>

  <h3>Print Preview</h3>
  <p>
    The forms are designed for <strong>Landscape A4</strong> paper. When you click <strong>"Print A4 Sheets"</strong>:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>A new window will open with the form(s) displayed.</li>
    <li>The browser's <strong>print dialog</strong> will appear automatically.</li>
    <li><strong>Check your print settings:</strong> make sure the page size is <strong>A4</strong> and orientation is <strong>Landscape</strong>.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="note success">
    <strong>📐 Important:</strong> If the form looks cut off or too small, adjust your browser's "Scale" setting in the print dialog to <strong>Fit to Page</strong> or <strong>100%</strong>.
  </div>

  <h3>Printing on Different Devices</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>💻 PC / Mac:</strong> Use <kbd>Ctrl+P</kbd> (Windows) or <kbd>Cmd+P</kbd> (Mac) after clicking "Print A4 Sheets".</li>
    <li><strong>📱 Android / iOS:</strong> Tap the <strong>menu</strong> (three dots) in the new window and select <strong>"Print"</strong>.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- ===== SECTION 5: PERFORMANCE ===== -->
  <h2>⏱️ Performance – Why It Might Take a Moment</h2>
  <p>
    Generating forms involves:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>🖼️ Loading background images (templates). If images are missing, the tool uses a <strong>white background</strong> as a fallback.</li>
    <li>📝 Placing every crew member's name, rank, and ID into the correct slots.</li>
    <li>🔄 Rendering all pages as high‑quality images.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>⏳ Depending on your device's processing power, this can take a few seconds.</strong>
    Older phones or tablets may take longer – this is normal. Please be patient and wait for the previews to appear.
  </div>

  <!-- ===== SECTION 6: FUTURE UPDATES ===== -->
  <h2>🚧 Future Updates – More Destinations & Forms</h2>
  <p>
    This tool is actively being improved.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>More destinations</strong> – we've already added HYD, BLR, AMD, ATQ on top of BOM and DEL.</li>
    <li><strong>More form types</strong> – for different Customs and Immigration requirements.</li>
    <li><strong>Saved settings</strong> – remember your fine‑tune adjustments.</li>
    <li><strong>PIC selection</strong> – choose the Captain for top‑page placement.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    I welcome every feedback, the tool will continue to improve based on your feedback. Don't hesitate to dm Alif or whatsapp call Fahrin.
  </p>

  <!-- ===== SECTION 7: TROUBLESHOOTING ===== -->
  <h2>❓ Troubleshooting – Common Issues</h2>

  <h3>❌ "Please parse a PDF first"</h3>
  <p>
    You haven't uploaded a PDF yet, or the upload failed. Click <span class="btn-upload-demo" style="font-size:13px; padding:4px 14px;">📎 Choose File</span> and select your CrewTripReport PDF.
  </p>

  <h3>❌ "No templates for this destination"</h3>
  <p>
    The destination you selected doesn't have any forms yet. Try selecting a different destination, or wait for a future update.
  </p>

  <h3>❌ The forms look blank (white background)</h3>
  <p>
    The background images may not have loaded. The tool automatically falls back to a <strong>white background</strong> so the text still appears – you can still use the forms, they'll just be blank paper.
    To get the proper template background, ensure the <code>templates/</code> folder is in the same directory as <code>CTR.html</code> and that the images are named correctly (e.g., <code>BOM_baggage.png</code>).
  </p>

  <h3>❌ Text is misaligned on the form</h3>
  <p>
    Use the <strong>fine‑tune sliders</strong> to adjust the text position. Each form has its own set of controls – adjust until it looks perfect.
  </p>

  <h3>❌ The builder won't show up</h3>
  <p>
    Make sure you tap the <span style="font-size:24px;">👷</span> emoji at the <strong>bottom of the page</strong> exactly <strong>7 times</strong> within 5 seconds (if you pause too long, the counter resets). After the 7th tap, the card will appear.
  </p>

